# Human Partial CDS Examples from NCBI RefSeq GRCh38.p14 (GCF_000001405.40)
#
# Context & Convention in NCBI RefSeq GFF3:
# Partial (incomplete) transcripts / CDSs represent truncated protein models (e.g., from EST/RNA-seq
# or genomic fragment boundaries).
# - Positive strand (+):
#   * 5' partial CDS: start_range=.,<start_pos>; may have initial phase (0, 1, or 2).
#   * 3' partial CDS: end_range=<end_pos>,.; terminal codon is truncated (no stop codon).
# - Negative strand (-):
#   * 5' partial CDS: truncated at the upper numerical genomic coordinate; annotated with
#     end_range=<upper_pos>,. and an initial reading phase offset (e.g. phase 2).
#   * 3' partial CDS: truncated at the lower numerical genomic coordinate; annotated with
#     start_range=.,<lower_pos>.
#
